$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A -Sequential Suzuki-Hiyama
Reaction i. To a 5 mL round bottomed flask equipped with a magnetic
stirrer bar and reflux condenser is added MIDA-vinyl silane 1, Pd(OAc)2
(5 mol%) SPhos (10 mol%) and aryl halide (1.2 equiv.) and the mixture
purged with argon for 5 min after which dioxane (0.08M) was added and the
solution stirred for a further 10 min. K3PO4 solution (7.5 equiv., 3M
solution degassed) was then added and the mixture stirred at 60 °C until
TLC analysis showed complete consumption of starting material (TLC eluted
with EtOAc). The mixture was diluted with DCM and passed through a pad of
Celite, washing with DCM and EtOAc and the solution concentrated. The
residue was redissolved in dry THF (1M), followed by the addition of the
requisite aryl iodide (1.5 eq). The mixture was purged under argon,
followed by the addition of TBAF (2 equiv, 1M in THF) and the resulting
mixture stirred at 25 °C for 30 min. Pd2dba3.CHCl3 (2.5 mol%) was then
added and the dark brown solution stirred at 25 °C for 6 hours. The
mixture was diluted with DCM, passed through a pad of Celite washing with
DCM and concentrated/ The residue was purified by flash column
chromatography to afford the requisite product.
(E)-1-methyl-4-styrylbenzene (4b). The title compound was prepared
according to general procedure A, using vinylborane 2 (38 mg, 0.12 mmol),
Pd(OAc)2 (1.3 mg, 5.7 μmol), SPhos (4.7 mg, 11.4 μmol), iodobenzene (28
mg, 0.14 mmol) and K3PO4 (0.28 mL, 0.86 mmol) in dioxane (1.4 mL) and
stirred at 60 °C overnight. After filtration through Celite,
concentration and redissolving the residue in THF (0.1 mL), 4-iodotoluene
(37 mg, 0.17 mmol) and TBAF (0.23 mL, 0.23 mmol) were added followed by
the addition of Pd2dba3.CHCl3 (3.0 mg, 2.9 μmol) and the mixture stirred
for 6 hours. Filtration through Celite and flash column chromatography.
(E)-1-fluoro-4-(4-methoxystyryl)benzene (4g). The title compound was
prepared according to general procedure A, using vinylborane 2 (40 mg,
0.12 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (1.4 mg, 6.0 μmol), SPhos (4.9 mg, 12 μmol),
4-iodoanisole (33 mg, 0.145 mmol) and K3PO4 (0.3 mL, 0.9 mmol) in dioxane
(1.5 mL) and stirred at 60 °C overnight. After filtration through Celite,
concentration and redissolving the residue in THF (0.1 mL),
4-Fluoroiodobenzene (40 mg, 0.18 mmol) and TBAF (0.24 mL, 0.24 mmol) were
added followed by the addition of Pd2dba3.CHCl3 (3.1 mg, 3.0 μmol) and
the mixture stirred for 6 hours. Filtration through Celite and flash
column chromatography. 4g (25 mg, 91%) as a white solid. Rf (10% Ethyl
Acetate:Hexane) = 0.63; 1H NMR: (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.61-7.54 (4H, m),
7.48 (2H, d, J = 8.5 Hz), 7.15 (1H, d, J = 16.1 Hz), 6.98 (1H, d, J =
16.1 Hz), 6.91 (2H, d, J = 8.7 Hz), 3.84 (3H, s);13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 162.4 (JC-F = 245 Hz), 159.6, 133.6 (JC-F = 3.5 Hz), 129.0, 127.7(JC-F
= 2.1 Hz), 127.6 (JC-F = 7.8 Hz) 127.6, 125.5, 115.3 (JC-F = 22.2 Hz),
109, 55.3. All spectra are in accordance to those previously reported.7
