$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for 53a-c. A stirred mixture
of 52c (20.4 g, 55.1 mmol, 53a synthesis) or 52c (19.0 g, 51.2 mmol, 53b
synthesis) or 52a (19.0 g, 53.6 mmol, 53c synthesis), the appropriate
boronic acid (1.1-1.6 equiv), Pd(PPh3)4 (0.05-0.1 equiv), and Na2CO3 (5.0
equiv) in acetonitrile-water (3:1) (0.1 M) was heated to 100 °C. After
1-4 days, the mixture was cooled to rt, concentrated, and partitioned
between DCM and water. The water layer (pH 10-11) was washed with DCM to
remove byproducts. The organic and acidic aqueous layers were separated.
The aqueous layer was treated with 2 N HCl (0.2 M in substrate) and
extracted with DCM. The organic layer was washed with water brine, dried
over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated.
2-((1S)-1-(8-Chloro-2-(2-fluorophenyl)quinolin-3-yl)-ethylcarbamoyl)benzoic
Acid (53b). Brown solid; yield 91% (20.9 g, 46.5 mmol). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
[D6]DMSO) δ ppm 12.86 (1 H, br. s), 8.92 (1 H, br s), 8.62 (1 H, s), 8.02
(1 H, dd, J = 8.4, 1.2 Hz), 7.96 (1 H, dd, J = 7.5, 1.3 Hz), 7.75(1 H,
dd, J = 7.5, 1.1 Hz), 7.53-7.67 (4 H, m), 2.03 (2 H, s), 7.46-7.52 (1 H,
m), 7.36-7.45 (3 H, m), 5.09 (1 H, quin, J = 6.9 Hz), 1.36 (3 H, d, J =
6.8 Hz). Mass spectrum (ESI) m/e = 449.0 (M + 1).
